2026-02-11 01:34:50,116 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document What Is the Difference Between Spot Markets and Futures Markets?

Forwards and futures are derivatives contracts that use the spot market as the underlying asset. These are contracts that give the owner control of the underlying at some point in the future, for a price agreed upon today. Only when the contracts expire would physical delivery of the commodity or other asset take place, and often traders will roll over or close out their contracts to avoid making or taking delivery altogether. Forwards and futures are generically the same, except that forwards are customizable and trade over the counter, whereas futures are standardized and traded on exchanges. is relevant
