2026-02-11 01:34:52,975 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document What Is the Spot Market?

The spot market refers to the trade of financial instruments for immediate payment and delivery. Assets traded in the spot market include commodities, currencies, and securities. Delivery occurs when the buyer and seller exchange cash for the financial instrument.

A futures contract, on the other hand, is based on the payment and delivery of the underlying asset at a future date. Exchanges and over-the-counter (OTC) markets may provide spot trading and/or futures trading. is relevant
